<title>TURKEY: Turkish Ziraat Bank to set up bank in Bosnia.</title>
<headline>Turkish Ziraat Bank to set up bank in Bosnia.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkey's biggest state-run Ziraat Bank will set up a new bank in Bosnia-Herzegovina, the official gazette said on Friday.</p>
<p>It said the cabinet approved Ziraat Bank's move to set up a fully-owned new bank with a Turkish name and 10 million mark capital in Bosnia.</p>
<p>Salih Sevki Doruk, acting deputy general manager of Ziraat, had earlier said the new bank would start operations as soon as a suitable building was chosen in Sarajevo.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-275 08 75</p>
</text>
